{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/711615-what-are-the-causes-for-death-among-kitsune-parents","id":711615,"title":"What are the causes for death among Kitsune parents?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-20T19:28:53-07:00","id":711615,"title":"What are the causes for death among Kitsune parents?","content":"If one were to try to fix the mortality problem among Kitsune regarding dead parents you would need to establish a cause for the problem. Can anyone think of a reason for why they are cursed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T19:42:18-07:00","id":711649,"title":"","content":"I don't look at it as a curse. It is a price for being the only breed that will breed true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T19:55:04-07:00","id":711673,"title":"","content":"I think somewhere in the mythology the &quot;fox spirit&quot; transfers from the parent to child, could be because they are so long lived.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T05:55:13-07:00","id":712289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/711615-what-are-the-causes-for-death-among-kitsune-parents#post711615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If one were to try to fix the mortality problem among Kitsune regarding dead parents you would need to establish a cause for the problem. Can anyone think of a reason for why they are cursed?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Entropy, delcious entropy. Mate only with mages who will break all curses! Hedge magic also may effect probability but my Hedge Magic lore is not so good. EIther way Gaia clearly wants Kitsune to be the magic guys to watch the magick users so you know they should do this.<br /> <br /> <br /> Reason for the curse? Because the Game isn't WereFox the Apocalypse and unless you have a breeding cap on them Kitsune would be the most common changing Breed instead of inexplicably Asian only.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/711615-what-are-the-causes-for-death-among-kitsune-parents?p=711649#post711649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't look at it as a curse. It is a price for being the only breed that will breed true.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nagah breed True.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T07:19:50-07:00","id":712367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/711615-what-are-the-causes-for-death-among-kitsune-parents?p=712289#post712289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Entropy, delcious entropy. Mate only with mages who will break all curses! Hedge magic also may effect probability but my Hedge Magic lore is not so good. EIther way Gaia clearly wants Kitsune to be the magic guys to watch the magick users so you know they should do this.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not why they pick mages for this duty. It's because it's one less namebreaker and you get a new fox.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Reason for the curse? Because the Game isn't WereFox the Apocalypse and unless you have a breeding cap on them Kitsune would be the most common changing Breed instead of inexplicably Asian only. </div> </div> </div>Possibly not, given cultural reasons not to go too far out, increased mortality as they become more common, or breeding restrictions like the Same-Bito used to be stated as having (twice per century). There's a lot of metatextual consideration that could go into removing it and replacing it with something else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nagah breed True. </div> </div> </div>Once per Naginah per lifetime. The rest of the kids are up in the air.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T10:24:51-07:00","id":712639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/711615-what-are-the-causes-for-death-among-kitsune-parents?p=712367#post712367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Possibly not, given cultural reasons not to go too far out, increased mortality as they become more common, or breeding restrictions like the Same-Bito used to be stated as having (twice per century). There's a lot of metatextual consideration that could go into removing it and replacing it with something else.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Its my big complaint, Kitsune should be a common changing Breed. There are more legends about Fox changers through out Asian cultures than I have ever read about a &quot;were rat&quot;(which i am pretty sure was made up for D&amp;D). They should have been the one with Asian Flavor that spread through out the world. But because Asia is &quot;Mysterious&quot; so they have to be rarer.<br /> <br /> With How common foxes are it comes up as pretty silly.<br /> <br /> <br /> As For Kitsune breeding true, it only happens 1 in 10 times anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","user":"Lian","date":". 10-21-2015, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T13:53:31-07:00","id":712984,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately, how common a species is has bugger all to do with the geographical spread or common-ness of the related shapeshifter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T15:46:40-07:00","id":713108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/711615-what-are-the-causes-for-death-among-kitsune-parents?p=712984#post712984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately, how common a species is has bugger all to do with the geographical spread or common-ness of the related shapeshifter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Really? Because its pretty much the case for everything but Kitsune and Nagah. &quot;are there bears in a location?&quot; Then there's a Gurhal group there(except Asia). Are there wolves? Garou. The various Bastet tribes match up generally geographically where their beastkin are found. Now there are definately Changing breeds outside their Beastkins' territory but only the Kitsune and Nagah have the Beastkin outside their traditional territory.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T16:52:14-07:00","id":713194,"title":"","content":"Yep, really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T17:30:59-07:00","id":713294,"title":"","content":"there are werewolves in places wolves dont live, like australia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7141-nasrudin","name":"Nasrudin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T17:47:49-07:00","id":713326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nasrudin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/711615-what-are-the-causes-for-death-among-kitsune-parents?p=713294#post713294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">there are werewolves in places wolves dont live, like australia.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> that's the exact opposite of what I am saying. Generally the traditional places wolves are has werewolves. There's not a huge gap where there were wolves but no werewolves. Most changers can be found in traditional area PLUS outside areas like werewolves in Australia. Kitsune and Nagah are the only ones who don't hit their beastkin range","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T23:11:51-07:00","id":713791,"title":"","content":"I feel a bit silly for having spent so much time looking into this and working out ways to explain it when writing for Shattered Dreams then. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Basically, I'm on your side here. It irks me that the Hengeyokai have no name for Apis, Grondr and Camazotz, for example, when all those Breeds should have made at least as much impression as the Okuma. And why are there no South American Garou? And when's the last time you heard of a Hengeyokai Qualmi? Or a Middle-Eastern Swara? Or Indian Swara? Or Thai Swara? Indian Ajaba? Or Siberian Ajaba? And how could Khara shapeshifters even exist if Sabertooths only inhabited North America and died out long before any humans got there?<br /> <br /> So yeah, it's not just Nagah and Kitsune who don't live everywhere they have related kin animals. And yeah, it's something I don't like not having explanations for. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T23:59:54-07:00","id":713817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/711615-what-are-the-causes-for-death-among-kitsune-parents?p=713791#post713791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel a bit silly for having spent so much time looking into this and working out ways to explain it when writing for Shattered Dreams then. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Basically, I'm on your side here. It irks me that the Hengeyokai have no name for Apis, Grondr and Camazotz, for example, when all those Breeds should have made at least as much impression as the Okuma. And why are there no South American Garou? And when's the last time you heard of a Hengeyokai Qualmi? Or a Middle-Eastern Swara? Or Indian Swara? Or Thai Swara? Indian Ajaba? Or Siberian Ajaba? And how could Khara shapeshifters even exist if Sabertooths only inhabited North America and died out long before any humans got there?<br /> <br /> So yeah, it's not just Nagah and Kitsune who don't live everywhere they have related kin animals. And yeah, it's something I don't like not having explanations for. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It was back to the Future day earlier. All I ask is you travel back in time and remove the Kitsune curse and make them a more standard changing breed!(j/k) honestly all those other additions make me feel better about the situation though I do feel that the Kitsune &quot;explanation&quot; comes off as a need to Mysteriousize the orient, rather than allow it to be a normal part of the setting. Foxes and Snakes have such a big footprint on human cultures through out the world, Kitsune myths can kind of match up with the whole Kin stock breeding true setup.<br /> <br /> Its so frustrating.. especially when I'm sure &quot;Wererats&quot; comes from D&amp;D.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T02:43:12-07:00","id":714058,"title":"","content":"Um, where is all this stuff about Nagah not having kin all over the world coming from? The Breedbook places them everywhere, mixing with practically all venmous snakes ever. It does claim that their most powerful Caerns are in India, but they're everywhere and practically breeding with everything.<br /> <br /> Also, there are Indian Simba and Swara. There are shifters wherever their animals are. Just because the breedbooks fixated on small chunks of the world, doesn't mean that there are no shifters of that type elsewhere.<br /> <br /> The same applies for Kitsune really, even though they will probably be rarer in the west then in the east... I'm sure that a Kitsune traveller could have fathered the lone Renards or Brother Foxes in Europe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T04:13:33-07:00","id":714133,"title":"","content":"Absolutely true! You could easily have (say) a Mexican Kitsune character. But I think the basic argument is about representation in canon. If a Breed never has kin or archetypes or auspices or tribes or names from Area-A, then it comes across as that breed doesn't live in Area-A.<br /> <br /> If Area-A is somewhere the animal kin would normally range, then it becomes really weird - here's a perfectly viable habitat for the Breed that never gets a mention, ergo the Breed doesn't come from there, but the animal kin are there, so... they should... and round and round and round.<br /> <br /> And note it also works in reverse - if a breedbook which is nominally the definitive guide to the whole breed around the world says everything about the Breed comes from Area-B and ignores Area-A, then it comes across as Area-A is weirdly unpopulated by the Breed and Area-B is EVERYTHING.<br /> <br /> Now, realistically it's simply because of time and word count pressures upon the authors. But then later info builds upon initial info which leads to the same merry-go-round saying the Breed comes from Area-B and never mentioning the equally valid Area-A. And then too some stressed frantically typing author will end up saying such things are literally true.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's pretty obvious (I think) that the reason the Hengeyokai book doesn't mention the Apis, Grondr or Camazotz is not because those breeds weren't theoretically present but because the author(s) didn't even know about those breeds to mention them. Or if they knew of them, certainly knew nothing about them other than 'Werewolves in the west killed them off at some point in the past'.<br /> <br /> Hence I've tried to be more inclusive, and/or, worked out reasons why populations are as they are presented. Even as simple a thing as giving an appropriate local name makes a big difference imo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-ni